<section class="story">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/abox/assembly.JPG", "A-BOX assembly" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Rugged Audio Box</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        A-BOX started as a simple idea: build a portable speaker that felt more like a small piece
        of equipment than a fragile consumer device.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        The enclosure shaped most decisions, from speaker placement and access panels to the internal
        routing of wiring and power electronics.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story story--reverse">
  <div class="container story__grid">
    <figure class="media media--4x3">
      {% img "assets/images/projects/abox/pcb1.jpeg", "A-BOX PCB work" %}
    </figure>

    <div class="story__content">
      <h2 class="story__title">Electronics</h2>
      <p class="story__text">
        The build included component selection, internal wiring, power management decisions and a small
        custom PCB effort to keep the final assembly cleaner.
      </p>
      <p class="story__text">
        It was an early but valuable exercise in making electronics physically robust, not just functional
        on a table.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="story">
